              "name": "bash",
              "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cat > /tmp/gh-aw/agent/libraries_new.md << 'ENDOFLIBRARIES'\\n# .NET Libraries in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n.NET 11 Preview 3 includes new .NET Libraries features & enhancements:\\n\\n- [System.Text.Json naming policy additions](#systemtextjson-naming-policy-additions)\\n- [Unsafe Evolution attributes](#unsafe-evolution-attributes)\\n- [SafeFileHandle.CreateAnonymousPipe](#safefilehandlecreateanonymouspipe)\\n- [WebProxy credentials from URI userinfo](#webproxy-credentials-from-uri-userinfo)\\n- [Parameterized CRC-32 and CRC-64](#parameterized-crc-32-and-crc-64)\\n\\n.NET Libraries updates in .NET 11:\\n\\n- [What's new in .NET 11](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/core/whats-new/dotnet-11/overview) documentation\\n\\n## System.Text.Json naming policy additions\\n\\n### `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase`\\n\\nA new built-in `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` converts property names to PascalCase (UpperCamelCase). This complements the existing `CamelCase`, `SnakeCaseLower`, `SnakeCaseUpper`, `KebabCaseLower`, and `KebabCaseUpper` policies and is particularly useful when working with JSON sources that use PascalCase property names. ([dotnet/runtime #124644](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/124644))\\n\\n```csharp\\nvar options = new JsonSerializerOptions\\n{\\n    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase\\n};\\n\\n// Serializes as {\\\"FirstName\\\":\\\"Jane\\\",\\\"LastName\\\":\\\"Doe\\\"}\\nstring json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new { firstName = \\\"Jane\\\", lastName = \\\"Doe\\\" }, options);\\n```\\n\\n`JsonKnownNamingPolicy.PascalCase` is the corresponding enum value for source-generated serialization contexts.\\n\\n### `[JsonNamingPolicy]` attribute\\n\\nA new `[JsonNamingPolicy]` attribute applies a naming policy to a single property, overriding the serializer's global policy for that member. ([dotnet/runtime #124645](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/124645))\\n\\n```csharp\\npublic class Config\\n{\\n    [JsonNamingPolicy(JsonKnownNamingPolicy.SnakeCaseLower)]\\n    public string DatabaseHost { get; set; } = \\\"\\\";  // serializes as \\\"database_host\\\"\\n\\n    public string ApiKey { get; set; } = \\\"\\\";         // uses global policy\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Unsafe Evolution attributes\\n\\n> This is a preview feature for .NET 11.\\n\\nNew attributes in `System.Runtime.CompilerServices` let API authors annotate unsafe contracts at the declaration site, improving tooling diagnostics and documentation for code that works with unmanaged memory or low-level runtime interfaces. ([dotnet/runtime #125721](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125721))\\n\\nThese attributes are part of the Unsafe Evolution initiative, which aims to give developers structured ways to express and reason about safety boundaries without requiring separate documentation.\\n\\n## SafeFileHandle.CreateAnonymousPipe\\n\\n`SafeFileHandle.CreateAnonymousPipe` is a new static factory method that creates a pair of `SafeFileHandle` objects for an anonymous pipe. Each end can be independently configured for async or synchronous I/O, and non-blocking I/O is supported on Unix. ([dotnet/runtime #125220](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125220))\\n\\n```csharp\\nSafeFileHandle.CreateAnonymousPipe(\\n    out SafeFileHandle readHandle,\\n    out SafeFileHandle writeHandle,\\n    asyncRead: true,\\n    asyncWrite: false);\\n\\nawait using var reader = new FileStream(readHandle, FileAccess.Read, bufferSize: 4096, isAsync: true);\\nusing var writer = new FileStream(writeHandle, FileAccess.Write);\\n```\\n\\nThe API works on Windows and Unix. On Windows, `Process.StandardInput`, `StandardOutput`, and `StandardError` now use this method for more reliable async I/O with child processes.\\n\\n### RandomAccess on non-seekable files\\n\\n`RandomAccess.Read` and `RandomAccess.Write` now accept non-seekable file handles. Calling these methods on a pipe or character device no longer throws; the underlying OS call proceeds as expected. ([dotnet/runtime #125512](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125512))\\n\\n## WebProxy credentials from URI userinfo\\n\\n`WebProxy` now reads credentials directly from the userinfo component of the proxy URI. ([dotnet/runtime #125384](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125384))\\n\\n```csharp\\n// Credentials are parsed automatically from the URI\\nvar proxy = new WebProxy(\\\"******proxy.example.com:8080\\\");\\n\\n// Before: credentials had to be set separately\\nvar proxy = new WebProxy(\\\"http://proxy.example.com:8080\\\")\\n{\\n    Credentials = new NetworkCredential(\\\"user\\\", \\\"pass\\\")\\n};\\n```\\n\\n## Parameterized CRC-32 and CRC-64\\n\\nNew `Crc32` and `Crc64` constructors accept a polynomial, initial value, and bit-reflection options, enabling computation of any standard or custom CRC variant. Previously only the standard CRC-32/ISO-HDLC and CRC-64/ECMA-182 presets were available. ([dotnet/runtime](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/commit/832a1600f6c41c3a91f80b8c4bc4194dc21338e2))\\n\\nCustom polynomial CRC computation is now SIMD-vectorized on x64 and ARM64, matching the throughput of the preset implementations. ([dotnet/runtime](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/commit/d560dfc45e65f314f5dfef6b30c7f58e3e5e87c1))\\n\\nZIP archive reading now validates CRC32 checksums, catching silent data corruption. ([dotnet/runtime #124766](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/124766))\\n\\n## Performance\\n\\n### `HashSet<T>` lookup and insert\\n\\nThe JIT now eliminates bounds checks in `HashSet<T>` lookup and insertion hot paths, reducing instruction count and improving throughput for collection-heavy workloads. ([dotnet/runtime #125893](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125893))\\n\\n### `TensorPrimitives.Asin`\\n\\n`TensorPrimitives.Asin` is now SIMD-vectorized using new `Vector128<T>.Asin()` and `Vector256<T>.Asin()` methods, improving throughput for machine learning and signal-processing workloads on x64 and ARM64. ([dotnet/runtime #126052](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/126052))\\n\\n## Other improvements\\n\\n- **DNS** — The DNS resolver now correctly handles RFC 6761 special-use domain names (`.local`, `.localhost`, `.invalid`, and others), returning the specified stub results instead of forwarding to the upstream resolver. ([dotnet/runtime #123076](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/123076))\\n- **Process** — `ProcessStartInfo` constructor and `Process.Start` now accept `null` for the `fileName` and `arguments` parameters, simplifying nullable-aware code patterns. ([dotnet/runtime #126076](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/126076))\\n- **Hot reload** — A new `DOTNET_HOTRELOAD_DISABLE` environment variable fully disables the hot-reload infrastructure at startup. ([dotnet/runtime #123744](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/123744))\\n- **Tar** — `TarWriter` now emits `HardLink` entries when writing multiple entries that share the same inode, producing spec-compliant archives with hard-linked files. ([dotnet/runtime #123874](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/123874))\\n- **NativeAOT** — Publishing a NativeAOT app with `EmbedUntrackedSatelliteAssemblies=true` no longer also includes uncompressed copies of those assemblies in the output, fixing unexpected binary size growth. ([dotnet/runtime #124192](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/124192))\\n- **COM interop** — New simplified `ComWrappers` APIs reduce boilerplate for common COM interop scenarios. ([dotnet/runtime #120114](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/120114))\\n\\n<!-- Filtered features (significant engineering work, but too niche for release notes):\\n  - [Wasm RyuJIT] codegen improvements for struct locals and register-sized structs: Internal JIT improvements for WASM; not directly user-visible.\\n  - cDAC: GetArgumentByIndex, GetLocalVariableByIndex, GetName, ClrDataFrame: Runtime diagnostics internals; developers don't target cDAC APIs directly.\\n  - SVE2 non-temporal scatter/gather stores and Counting APIs: ARM64 SVE2 intrinsics; too narrow for general audience.\\n  - Profile optimization for single-file deployment: Niche (single-file + profile-guided optimization); low outside engagement.\\n  - [Android CoreCLR] Managed callstack logging on native crash: Narrow platform scenario.\\n-->\\n\\n## Community contributors\\n\\nThank you to everyone who contributed to .NET 11 Preview 3! ❤️\\nENDOFLIBRARIES\\necho \\\"Written $(wc -l < /tmp/gh-aw/agent/libraries_new.md) lines\\\"\", \"description\": \"Write new libraries.md\"}"
