onNamingPolicy(JsonKnownNamingPolicy.SnakeCaseLower)]\\n    public string DatabaseHost { get; set; } = \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\";  // serializes as \\\\\\\"database_host\\\\\\\"\\n    public string ApiKey { get; set; } = \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\";         // uses global policy\\n}\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\n## Unsafe Evolution attributes\\n\\n> This is a preview feature for .NET 11.\\n\\nNew attributes in \\\\`System.Runtime.CompilerServices\\\\` let API authors annotate unsafe contracts at the declaration site, improving tooling diagnostics for code that works with unmanaged memory or low-level runtime interfaces. These attributes are part of the Unsafe Evolution preview initiative. ([dotnet/runtime #125721](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125721))\\n\\n## SafeFileHandle.CreateAnonymousPipe\\n\\n\\\\`SafeFileHandle.CreateAnonymousPipe\\\\` is a new static factory method that creates a pair of \\\\`SafeFileHandle\\\\` objects for an anonymous pipe. Each end can be independently configured for async or synchronous I/O, with non-blocking I/O supported on Unix. ([dotnet/runtime #125220](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125220))\\n\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`csharp\\nSafeFileHandle.CreateAnonymousPipe(\\n    out SafeFileHandle readHandle,\\n    out SafeFileHandle writeHandle,\\n    asyncRead: true,\\n    asyncWrite: false);\\n\\nawait using var reader = new FileStream(readHandle, FileAccess.Read, bufferSize: 4096, isAsync: true);\\nusing var writer = new FileStream(writeHandle, FileAccess.Write);\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\nThe API works on Windows and Unix. On Windows, \\\\`Process.StandardInput\\\\`, \\\\`StandardOutput\\\\`, and \\\\`StandardError\\\\` now use this method for more reliable async I/O with child processes.\\n\\n### RandomAccess on non-seekable files\\n\\n\\\\`RandomAccess.Read\\\\` and \\\\`RandomAccess.Write\\\\` now accept non-seekable file handles. Calling these methods on a pipe or character device no longer throws; the underlying OS call proceeds as expected. ([dotnet/runtime #125512](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125512))\\n\\n## WebProxy credentials from URI userinfo\\n\\n\\\\`WebProxy\\\\` now reads credentials directly from the userinfo component of the proxy URI. ([dotnet/runtime #125384](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125384))\\n\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`csharp\\n// Credentials are parsed automatically from the URI\\nvar proxy = new WebProxy(\\\\\\\"******proxy.example.com:8080\\\\\\\");\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\n## Parameterized CRC-32 and CRC-64\\n\\nNew constructors for \\\\`Crc32\\\\` and \\\\`Crc64\\\\` accept a polynomial, initial value, and bit-reflection options, enabling computation of any standard or custom CRC variant. Previously only the default CRC-32/ISO-HDLC and CRC-64/ECMA-182 presets were available. ([dotnet/runtime](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/commit/832a1600f6c41c3a91f80b8c4bc4194dc21338e2))\\n\\nCustom polynomial CRC computation is now SIMD-vectorized on x64 and ARM64, matching the throughput of the preset implementations. ([dotnet/runtime](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/commit/d560dfc45e65f314f5dfef6b30c7f58e3e5e87c1))\\n\\nZIP archive reading now validates CRC32 checksums against stored values. ([dotnet/runtime #124766](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/124766))\\n\\n## Performance\\n\\n### \\\\`HashSet<T>\\\\` lookup and insert\\n\\nThe JIT now eliminates bounds checks in \\\\`HashSet<T>\\\\` lookup and insertion hot paths, reducing instruction count for collection-heavy workloads. ([dotnet/runtime #125893](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125893))\\n\\n### \\\\`TensorPrimitives.Asin\\\\`\\n\\n\\\\`TensorPrimitives.Asin\\\\` is now SIMD-vectorized via new \\\\`Vector128<T>.Asin()\\\\` and \\\\`Vector256<T>.Asin()\\\\` methods, benefiting ML and signal-processing workloads on x64 and ARM64. ([dotnet/runtime #126052](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/126052))\\n\\n## Other improvements\\n\\n- **DNS** — The DNS resolver now correctly handles RFC 6761 special-use domain names (`.local`, `.localhost`, `.invalid`), returning the correct stub results instead of forwarding to the upstream resolver. ([dotnet/runtime #123076](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/123076))\\n- **Process** — \\\\`ProcessStartInfo\\\\` constructor and \\\\`Process.Start\\\\` now accept \\\\`null\\\\` for \\\\`fileName\\\\` and \\\\`arguments\\\\` parameters. ([dotnet/runtime #126076](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/126076))\\n- **Hot reload** — A new \\\\`DOTNET_HOTRELOAD_DISABLE\\\\` environment variable fully disables hot-reload infrastructure at startup. ([dotnet/runtime #123744](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/123744))\\n- **Tar** — \\\\`TarWriter\\\\` now emits \\\\`HardLink\\\\` entries when writing files that share the same inode, producing spec-compliant archives. ([dotnet/runtime #123874](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/123874))\\n- **NativeAOT** — Publishing with \\\\`EmbedUntrackedSatelliteAssemblies=true\\\\` no longer includes uncompressed copies of those assemblies, fixing unexpected binary size growth. ([dotnet/runtime #124192](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/124192))\\n- **COM interop** — New simplified \\\\`ComWrappers\\\\` APIs reduce boilerplate for common COM interop scenarios. ([dotnet/runtime #120114](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/120114))\\n\\n<!-- Filtered features (significant engineering work, but too niche for release notes):\\n  - HashSet<T> / Dictionary<T>: Dictionary.Remove codegen improvement was not confirmed shipped.\\n  - [Wasm RyuJIT] codegen: Internal JIT improvements for WASM; not directly user-visible.\\n  - cDAC diagnostic APIs: Runtime internals; developers do not target cDAC directly.\\n  - SVE2 scatter/gather and Counting APIs: ARM64 SVE2 intrinsics; narrow audience.\\n-->\\n\\n## Community contributors\\n\\nThank you to everyone who contributed to .NET 11 Preview 3! ❤️\\n'''\\nwith open('release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/libraries.md', 'w') as f:\\n    f.write(content)\\nprint('libraries.md written')\\n\\\"\", \"description\": \"Write new libraries.md using Python\"}"
