              "arguments": "{\"new_str\": \"## WebProxy credentials from URI userinfo\\n\\n`WebProxy` now reads credentials directly from the userinfo component of the proxy URI. ([dotnet/runtime #125384](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125384))\\n\\n```csharp\\n// Credentials are parsed automatically from the URI\\nvar proxy = new WebProxy(\\\"******proxy.example.com:8080\\\");\\n```\\n\\n## Parameterized CRC-32 and CRC-64\\n\\nNew constructors for `Crc32` and `Crc64` accept a polynomial, initial value, and bit-reflection options, enabling computation of any standard or custom CRC variant. Previously only the default CRC-32/ISO-HDLC and CRC-64/ECMA-182 presets were available. ([dotnet/runtime](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/commit/832a1600f6c41c3a91f80b8c4bc4194dc21338e2))\\n\\nCustom polynomial CRC computation is now SIMD-vectorized on x64 and ARM64, matching the throughput of the preset implementations. ([dotnet/runtime](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/commit/d560dfc45e65f314f5dfef6b30c7f58e3e5e87c1))\\n\\nZIP archive reading now validates CRC32 checksums against stored values, catching silent data corruption. ([dotnet/runtime #124766](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/124766))\", \"old_str\": \"## WebProxy credentials from URI userinfo\\n\\n`WebProxy` now reads credentials directly from the userinfo component of the proxy URI, eliminating the need to set `Credentials` separately. ([dotnet/runtime #125384](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125384))\\n\\n```csharp\\n// Before: separate Credentials assignment needed\\nvar proxy = new WebProxy(\\\"http://proxy.example.com:8080\\\")\\n{\\n    Credentials = new NetworkCredential(\\\"user\\\", \\\"pass\\\")\\n};\\n\\n// After: credentials parsed from URI automatically\\nvar proxy = new WebProxy(\\\"******proxy.example.com:8080\\\");\\n```\", \"path\": \"/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/libraries.md\"}"
            }
          }
