              "name": "edit",
              "arguments": "{\"new_str\": \"## Performance\\n\\n### `HashSet<T>` lookup and insert\\n\\nThe JIT now eliminates bounds checks in `HashSet<T>` lookup and insertion hot paths, reducing instruction count for collection-heavy workloads. ([dotnet/runtime #125893](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125893))\\n\\n### `TensorPrimitives.Asin`\\n\\n`TensorPrimitives.Asin` is now SIMD-vectorized via new `Vector128<T>.Asin()` and `Vector256<T>.Asin()` methods, benefiting ML and signal-processing workloads on x64 and ARM64. ([dotnet/runtime #126052](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/126052))\\n\\n## Other improvements\\n\\n- **DNS** — The DNS resolver now correctly handles RFC 6761 special-use domain names (`.local`, `.localhost`, `.invalid`), returning the correct stub results instead of forwarding to the upstream resolver. ([dotnet/runtime #123076](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/123076))\\n- **Process** — `ProcessStartInfo` constructor and `Process.Start` now accept `null` for `fileName` and `arguments` parameters. ([dotnet/runtime #126076](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/126076))\\n- **Hot reload** — A new `DOTNET_HOTRELOAD_DISABLE` environment variable fully disables hot-reload infrastructure at startup. ([dotnet/runtime #123744](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/123744))\\n- **Tar** — `TarWriter` now emits `HardLink` entries when writing files that share the same inode, producing spec-compliant archives. ([dotnet/runtime #123874](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/123874))\\n- **NativeAOT** — Publishing with `EmbedUntrackedSatelliteAssemblies=true` no longer includes uncompressed copies of those assemblies, fixing unexpected binary size growth. ([dotnet/runtime #124192](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/124192))\\n- **COM interop** — New simplified `ComWrappers` APIs reduce boilerplate for common COM interop scenarios. ([dotnet/runtime #120114](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/120114))\\n\\n## Bug fixes\", \"old_str\": \"## Performance\\n\\n### HashSet\\\\<T\\\\> and Dictionary\\\\<T\\\\> improvements\\n\\n`HashSet<T>` lookup and insertion operations benefit from JIT bounds-check elimination, reducing instruction count in the hot path. `Dictionary<T>.Remove` has been restructured to produce better codegen for value-type keys, reducing unnecessary branch overhead. ([dotnet/runtime #125893](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125893), [dotnet/runtime #125884](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125884))\\n\\n## Bug fixes\", \"path\": \"/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/libraries.md\"}"
