              "arguments": "{\"new_str\": \"# EF Core in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n.NET 11 Preview 3 includes EF Core updates:\\n\\n- [Cosmos DB: complex property querying](#cosmos-db-complex-property-querying)\\n- [Partial property loading](#partial-property-loading)\\n\\nFor EF Core updates in .NET 11:\\n\\n- [What's new in EF Core 11](https://learn.microsoft.com/ef/core/what-is-new/) documentation\\n\\n## Cosmos DB: complex property querying\\n\\nComplex properties stored as subdocuments in Azure Cosmos DB can now be used directly in LINQ `Where` clauses and projections. Previously, only top-level scalar properties were queryable using LINQ. ([dotnet/efcore #37577](https://github.com/dotnet/efcore/pull/37577), [dotnet/efcore #37919](https://github.com/dotnet/efcore/pull/37919))\\n\\n```csharp\\n// Address is a complex property stored as a subdocument\\nvar customers = await context.Customers\\n    .Where(c => c.Address.City == \\\"Seattle\\\")\\n    .ToListAsync();\\n```\\n\\n## Partial property loading\\n\\nEF Core can now load individual properties on demand after the initial query. This is useful when an entity has large blob or computed properties that are expensive to load for every row. ([dotnet/efcore #37857](https://github.com/dotnet/efcore/pull/37857))\\n\\n```csharp\\n// Load just the thumbnail initially\\nvar products = await context.Products\\n    .Select(p => new { p.Id, p.Name })\\n    .ToListAsync();\\n\\n// Load the full image only when needed\\nawait context.Entry(product).Property(p => p.FullImage).LoadAsync();\\n```\\n\", \"old_str\": \"# EF Core in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\nNo significant EF Core feature changes are highlighted for Preview 3. This preview included internal cleanup and refactoring work in the EF Core Cosmos provider.\\n\\nFor EF Core updates in .NET 11:\\n\\n- [What's new in EF Core 11](https://learn.microsoft.com/ef/core/what-is-new/) documentation\", \"path\": \"/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/efcore.md\"}"
            }
          }
        ],
        "parsed": null
