              "arguments": "{\"new_str\": \"# C# in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n.NET 11 Preview 3 includes C# compiler and tooling improvements:\\n\\n- [File-based program automatic discovery](#file-based-program-automatic-discovery)\\n- [VBCSCompiler build cache](#vbcscompiler-build-cache)\\n\\nFor C# language updates in .NET 11:\\n\\n- [What's new in C#](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/csharp/whats-new/) documentation\\n\\n## File-based program automatic discovery\\n\\nThe C# compiler now automatically identifies standalone `.cs` files as file-based programs when they contain top-level statements and no project file. This enables simple scripts and file-based apps to be recognized and executed by tooling without explicit project scaffolding. ([dotnet/roslyn #82863](https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/pull/82863))\\n\\n## VBCSCompiler build cache\\n\\nThe `VBCSCompiler` server process now caches compilation artifacts between builds. Incremental builds that recompile unchanged files benefit from the cache, reducing redundant work in large solutions. ([dotnet/roslyn #82881](https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/pull/82881))\\n\", \"old_str\": \"# C# in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\nNo significant C# language feature changes are highlighted for Preview 3.\\n\\nFor C# language updates in .NET 11:\\n\\n- [What's new in C#](https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/csharp/whats-new/) documentation\", \"path\": \"/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/csharp.md\"}"
