              "name": "edit",
              "arguments": "{\"new_str\": \"# MSBuild in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\n.NET 11 Preview 3 includes MSBuild performance improvements:\\n\\n- [Worker node preference](#worker-node-preference)\\n- [ItemSpec modifier performance](#itemspec-modifier-performance)\\n- [Unix build session reuse](#unix-build-session-reuse)\\n\\nFor MSBuild updates, see the [MSBuild documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/visualstudio/msbuild/whats-new-msbuild-16-0).\\n\\n## Worker node preference\\n\\nMSBuild now respects the `BuildRequestDataFlags.PreferredWorkerNode` flag, giving callers a hint about which worker node should execute a build request. This enables tools that build multiple projects in parallel to reduce process-boundary round-trips and improve scheduling efficiency. ([dotnet/msbuild #13452](https://github.com/dotnet/msbuild/pull/13452))\\n\\n## ItemSpec modifier performance\\n\\n`ItemSpecModifier` evaluation — computing `%(Filename)`, `%(Extension)`, `%(Directory)`, and other built-in modifiers — has been optimized to avoid redundant string allocations when the same item is used repeatedly in a target. This benefits builds with large item lists and many `Transform` or `Copy` tasks. ([dotnet/msbuild #13386](https://github.com/dotnet/msbuild/pull/13386))\\n\\n## Unix build session reuse\\n\\nOn Linux and macOS, MSBuild now reuses existing build sessions across successive CLI invocations in the same shell, reducing the startup cost of `dotnet build` for repeated builds. ([dotnet/msbuild #13354](https://github.com/dotnet/msbuild/pull/13354))\\n\", \"old_str\": \"# MSBuild in .NET 11 Preview 3\\n\\nNo significant MSBuild changes are highlighted for Preview 3.\\n\\nFor MSBuild updates, see the [MSBuild documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/visualstudio/msbuild/whats-new-msbuild-16-0).\", \"path\": \"/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/msbuild.md\"}"
            }
